    "### 13. Conditional Expectation as L2 Projection\n",
    "The space of square-integrable random variables $L_2(\\Omega, \\mathcal{F}, P)$ is a Hilbert space with inner product $\\langle X, Y \\rangle = \\mathbb{E}[XY]$.\n",
    "Conditional expectation $g(X) = \\mathbb{E}[Y|X]$ is the orthogonal projection of $Y$ onto the subspace of $X$-measurable functions. This means it minimizes the mean squared error:\n",
    "$$\\mathbb{E}[Y|X] = \\arg\\min_{g} \\mathbb{E}[(Y - g(X))^2]$$\n",
    "This is why the optimal prediction in supervised regression under MSE loss is exactly the conditional expectation $\\mathbb{E}[Y|X]$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical explanation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 14. Fokker-Planck Equation\n",
    "For $dx_t = b(x_t) dt + \\sigma dW_t$, the probability density function $p(x, t)$ of the state $x_t$ evolves according to the Fokker-Planck PDE:\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial p(x, t)}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}[b(x) p(x, t)] + \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2} \\frac{\\partial^2 p(x, t)}{\\partial x^2}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
