   "source": [
    "### 15. Doob's Martingale Convergence Theorem\n",
    "Doob's Martingale Convergence Theorem states that if a martingale $X_n$ is bounded in $L_1$ (i.e., $\\sup_n \\mathbb{E}[|X_n|] < \\infty$), then $X_n$ converges pointwise almost surely to a limit random variable $X_\\infty$ as $n \\to \\infty$.\n",
    "In Bayesian statistics, likelihood ratios and posterior distributions form martingales as more data is observed. Doob's theorem guarantees that the posterior distribution will converge to a stable limit almost surely."
   ]
